// lexdb over TDS: wrong answers and gaps of the SQL Server door left by the documentation slices (KNOWN-ISSUES.md, second robustness slice), checked
// against SQL Server 2022 (generated by tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py robust2 from mssql_robust2_queries.txt): a recursive CTE under TOP with a WHERE, a join,
// a derived table or an outer aggregate over the limited query stops when the query has its rows (MAXRECURSION counting the levels it takes to get
// them: 530 when they are further; a CTE read twice is made whole; an error in a row the query does not read is not raised), integer literals'
// arithmetic overflowing (8115). Each batch runs with SET lexdb_batch off and on; each expect line: "same: " and the batch's result sets and counts,
// or its error number.
// expect: ok
// expect: (100)
// expect: same: i: 7;14;21
// expect: same: i: 7;14;21
